From 88287cff47240aa58b5f0fea5da08670f1e87df6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bradley Gleave <bradley@bradleytgpcoaching.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 00:45:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bind accepted Start to its session before preflight; obsolete
 refresh stands down (S4 R5 reimplementation)

Narrow successor to 2bcf1563 for the two material findings of the frozen R4
source reviews. No message, manifest or backend contract changes; no new
dependency; pairing is never disabled.

S4-R4-A-01 (MATERIAL): handleStartImport / handleStartIngest captured the
session generation only after the cold preflight refresh resolved. A pairing
acknowledged while that refresh was on the wire, or queued behind its rotation
persist on the state lock, became the run's owner: every ingest/progress/
complete went out under the replacement's bearer, and in the on-the-wire
interleaving the run broadcast "login required to import" although the
replacement was fine. The generation is now read synchronously at admission
(the router calls the handler before yielding), preflightOwnedSession(generation)
verifies the OWNING session's token via ownedAccessToken(generation), and a
session replaced during preflight is reported with the replaced detail and
nothing else touched; "login required" is broadcast only when the run's own
session is still current and could not mint.

S4-R4-A-02 / S4-R4B-01: a refresh requested for the obsolete run and admitted
behind the replacement's establish read and presented the replacement's
refresh token (rotating it). refreshAccessToken / getAccessToken take an
optional expectedGeneration: a bound run records the generation under the lock
at snapshot and stands down WITHOUT reading the token when it no longer
matches; a bound joiner accepts a shared run's result only if it minted for its
own session; callers bound to different sessions never share a run; unbound
callers keep the previous semantics and re-run after joining a run that stood
down. Both entrypoints, makeSender and completeIngest pass their generation. No
lock is held across network work; same-session coalescing is unchanged.

Regressions: test/session-ownership-preflight.spec.js (worker level: C3
barrier and C1 on both entrypoints, rejection/timeout, clear+re-establish,
pending-establish failure, ingest C2 and P-C pending admission, settlement 401,
rotation persist failure, unchanged-session controls) and
test/refresh-admission-epoch.spec.js (session level: bound stand-down, stale
caller, same-session coalescing, unbound joiner re-run, cross-session no-join,
pending-establish failure, clear+re-establish, cold getAccessToken).
